he SAME preflight; `{"started": false, ...verdict}` on any refusal — loud, never a silent partial launch; on `ok` every exchange group's engine run executes SEQUENTIALLY on the ONE single-flight background job, one lake one writer); the EXISTING `POST /api/v1/sweep/run` single-exchange surface is UNCHANGED in contract (still tested/used) except it now also accepts `acknowledge_sla_overrun` and inherits the SAME institutional `build_sweep_kwargs` flip. **HONEST ENVELOPE (Golden Rule #10):** the 1m-coverage/lake-invariants/futures/VIX arms are `O(symbols × months)` — cheap DISK PROBES, never O(bars); the derived-freshness arm is the one honestly-expensive `O(bars)` reuse (G1's own pre-existing cost, not new); `count_true_trials` is `O(|k_values|)` (tiny, not a literal constant-factor O(1), never falsely claimed as such); `estimator_calibration.json` has NO writer on `main` yet (P2's future job) — every estimate is honestly `estimate_basis="provisional"` today (R23 MEASURED-TIMING-ONLY); the multi-exchange fan-out is `O(#groups)` (≤2 today). **TESTS:** 4 new dedicated files (`tests/unit/test_engine_estimator_calibration.py`, `test_engine_sweep_estimator.py`, `test_engine_sweep_oneclick_preflight.py`, `test_dashboard_sweep_oneclick_route.py`) + `test_dashboard_sweep_runner.py` extended for the R5 regression pin + the fan-out functions — 173 tests (recounted via `pytest --collect-only -q` on exactly these 5 files after every fix round below; earlier drafts of this entry claimed 154, then 150, then 156, then 161, then 162, then 164, then 165, then 166, then 169, then 171, all stale — corrected here), 100.00% line+branch on all 4 touched/new modules (`estimator_calibration.py` 61/18, `sweep_estimator.py` 53/12, `sweep_oneclick_preflight.py` 132/48, `sweep_runner.py` 205/52 stmts/branches, 0 missing each, re-measured after every fix round below); `ruff check`/`ruff format --check` clean; `mypy --strict brutex` clean (364 source files); `pyright brutex tests` 0 errors. **HOSTILE-REVIEW FIX ROUND (4-agent — hot-path/security/correctness/cite-path, this same PR):** hot-path found `evaluate_disk_guard`'s full-lake footprint scan was being paid ONCE PER EXCHANGE GROUP inside `oneclick_preflight_for_plan` — fixed to compute it ONCE per logical plan and thread it into `run_oneclick_preflight` via a new `disk_decision` parameter, with the true O(files-in-lake) cost now stated in both docstrings (previously undocumented, a Golden Rule #10 gap); security found `estimator_calibration.py`'s `schema_version` check accepted a JSON `true` (bool/int aliasing) and its "never raises" contract missed `UnicodeDecodeError` on non-UTF-8 file content — both fixed; correctness found `clamp_sweep_window`'s degenerate-range collapse silently moved `start` with no disclosed `Clamp` (a false-OK for a wholly-future request landing on a real trading day) — fixed to always emit an honest `start` clamp entry; a zero-`sample_trials` calibration file was accepted as `calibrated=True` despite R23 requiring a REAL measurement — fixed to require `sample_trials > 0`; the estimator's axis counts did not de-duplicate repeated CSV tokens the engine itself dedupes at grid-construction time (`SweepGridConfig`'s `_dedup_seq`), silently over-counting trials for a request like `symbols="NIFTY,NIFTY"` — fixed via a new `_dedup_axis` helper; the multi-exchange fold dropped `nominal_condition_count`/`effective_condition_count` from its `estimator` sub-dict (present in the single-group shape) — fixed, taking the minimum effective count across groups. cite-path found the ledger's own citations understated: `DEC-SWEEP-PREFLIGHT-001` is ledger entry #663, not #658 as first drafted (fixed below), and the initially-drafted "DEC-INSTITUTIONAL-ONECLICK-001" parent-decree token + a `[[wiki-link]]`-style reference to operator/coordinator-side working documents do not resolve to any in-repo ledger header or file — reworded to name the operator's directive in prose without a fabricated DEC-ID (this is the corrected wording you are reading). A confirmed TOCTOU gap between the sweep-vs-pull exclusion PROBE and the actual launch (no lock is held across the gap — `probe_pull_singleflight` is explicitly documented as read-only/best-effort) is a DISCLOSED, not silently accepted, residual: closing it needs a real cross-process exclusion lock, which is out of THIS phase's scope (no such lock exists anywhere in the codebase yet) — named here for the coordinator, not routed around. Re-verified 100.00% line+branch + ruff/mypy --strict/pyright clean after every fix above. **ADVERSARIAL-REFUTER FIX ROUND (3-agent — fix-verification/fresh-eyes-full-diff/test-suite-integrity, this same PR, after the hostile-review round above):** a REAL crash was found and fixed — `clamp_sweep_window`'s one-sided-clamp version left a window ENTIRELY before the floor (e.g. `start=2015-01-01, end=2016-01-01`) with its unclamped, still-pre-floor `end` reaching the calendar walk, raising `HolidayDataUnavailableError`; rewritten to interval-INTERSECTION logic (compute `[floor, ceiling]` once, collapse the WHOLE window to the nearest boundary when there is no overlap at all, otherwise clamp each side independently) — pinned by two new regression tests (`test_clamp_window_entirely_before_floor_collapses_without_crashing`, `test_clamp_window_entirely_after_ceiling_collapses_without_crashing`); a duplicate-symbol bug was found — `run_oneclick_preflight` iterated raw (non-deduplicated) `symbols`, so `symbols=["NIFTY","NIFTY"]` appended the SAME lake-invariant `Refusal` twice and re-paid its O(files) scan twice — fixed with a `dict.fromkeys()` dedup at the top of the function, pinned by `test_duplicate_symbol_is_not_double_refused`; two "never raises" gaps in `estimator_calibration.py` were found and closed — an unbounded `read_text()` could raise `MemoryError` on an adversarially large file (now capped at `_MAX_FILE_BYTES` = 64 KiB, plus a `path.is_file()` guard against directories/FIFOs/sockets)